lesson: 114
title: A pattern day by day
stars: 0
explain: When something grows by the same number each day, the first day has the start, and each later day adds the step once more.
explain: On day N the step has been added N - 1 times: start + (N - 1) × step.
explain: If Lily reads 5 pages on day 1 and 3 more each day than the day before, on day 6 she reads 5 + 5 × 3 = 20 pages.
vars: a=name s=2..10 k=2..6 d=3..10
answer: s + (d - 1) * k
exercise: On the first day {a} reads {s} pages. Each day {a.he} reads {k} more pages than the day before. How many pages does {a.he} read on the {d.ord} day?
exercise: {a} does {s} push-ups on day 1. Every day {a.he} does {k} more than the day before. How many push-ups does {a.he} do on day {d}?
exercise: A plant is {s} cm tall on the first day and grows {k} cm every day. How tall is it on the {d.ordwords} day?
exercise: On Monday {a} saves {s} dollars. Each day after that {a.he} saves {k} dollars more than the day before. How many dollars does {a.he} save on the {d.ord} day?
exercise: {a} runs {s} laps on day 1, and each day {k} laps more than the day before. How many laps does {a.he} run on day {d}?
exercise: A baker makes {s} cakes on the first day and {k} more cakes each day than the day before. How many cakes does the baker make on day {d}?
test: Day 1: {s} birds at the pond. Day 2: {s+k} birds. Day 3: {s+2*k} birds. If this goes on, how many birds are there on day {d}?
test: Every day {a} writes {k} more words in {a.his} diary than the day before. On the first day {a.he} wrote {s} words. How many words does {a.he} write on the {d.ordwords} day?
test: A row of towers is built from blocks: the first tower has {s} blocks, and each tower has {k} blocks more than the one before it. How many blocks are in tower number {d}?
test: How many shells does {a} find on day {d}, if {a.he} finds {s} on day 1, {s+k} on day 2 and {s+2*k} on day 3, always {k} more?
exercise: {a} from Iowa reads {s} pages on day 1 and every day {k} pages more than the day before. How many pages does {a.he} read on day {d}?
exercise: A sunflower is {s} cm tall on day 1 and grows {k} cm each day. How tall is it on day {d}?
exercise: On day {d}, how many laps does {a} swim if {a.he} swims {s} laps on day 1 and {k} more each day than the day before?
exercise: Day 1: {s} stamps. Each new day: {k} more stamps than the day before. How many stamps on day {d}?
exercise: {a} in Wales saves {s} pounds on the first day and {k} pounds more each day than the day before. How many pounds does {a.he} save on the {d.ordwords} day?
exercise: A bakery in Toronto sells {s} pies on day one, and each day it sells {k} more pies than the day before. How many pies does it sell on the {d.ord} day?
exercise: {a} does {s} sit-ups on day 1 and adds {k} sit-ups every day. How many sit-ups does {a.he} do on day {d}?
exercise: Each day a puppy in Brisbane walks {k} minutes longer than the day before. On day 1 it walks {s} minutes. How many minutes does it walk on day {d}?
test: A stack has {s} blocks on day 1, and {k} more blocks are added on each later day. How many blocks are in the stack on day {d}?
test: {a} from Auckland plants {s} seeds on the first day. On every next day {a.he} plants {k} seeds more than the day before. How many seeds does {a.he} plant on day {d}?
test: How many emails does {a} get on the {d.ordwords} day, if the count goes {s}, {s+k}, {s+2*k}, and so on?
test: In Dublin a choir has {s} singers at the first practice and {k} more at each practice after that. How many singers come to practice number {d}?
test: A snail is {s} cm up a wall on day 1 and {k} cm higher every day after. How many cm up the wall is it on day {d}?
test: {a} skips rope {s} times on day one and then {k} times more each day than the day before. How many times does {a.he} skip on the {d.ord} day?
