exam: It is given that {a} reads {s} pages on the first day and on each subsequent day {k} pages more than on the preceding day. Determine the number of pages read on the {d.ordwords} day.
exam: Ascertain the number of push-ups performed by {a} on day {d}, whereas {s} are performed on day 1 and the number increases by {k} each day.
exam: Whereas a sequence commences with {s} and each term exceeds the preceding term by {k}, state the {d.ordwords} term of the said sequence.
exam: Compute the quantity saved by {a} on the {d.ord} day, given a saving of {s} dollars on the first day and an increase of {k} dollars per day thereafter.
exercise: Since Grandad passed away, {a} walks his old dog every day. On day 1 they walk {s} minutes, and each day {k} minutes more than the day before. How many minutes do they walk on day {d}?
exercise: {a}'s mum was let go from her job. She sends {s} job letters on the first day and {k} more each day than the day before. How many letters does she send on the {d.ord} day?
